Subject: [PATCH] vayu_wifi W24d: parse the HTT in-order rx msdu (desc + native wifi), EAPOL-Key diagnostics

Base: W24K source (/mnt/ramdisk/w23/src at 2026-11-01 20:53, kernel mach-wifi-w24k.bin sha256
ab440b26e2051c4f1cf1f900a18b134b09f8b87460bd74f05537abfc0066375c). W24a..W24k have NO patch file in
this directory (0027, 0029, 0030 are missing); this diff is relative to W24K, not to W23b (0026).

Evidence (gunwest ~/ws-qup-hwcg/logs/193128-run.log, W24C): the "00 00 00 00 43 00 30 82 ..." dumps
were taken at buf+0 (len 2048), i.e. the rx descriptor, not the payload:
  word1 attention 0x82300043 = MSDU_DONE|DIRECTED|DA/SA_IDX_INVALID|NON_QOS|LAST|FIRST (no errors)
  word4 mpdu_start 0x70NN0866: peer 0x66, FROM_DS, seq NN = 2,3,4,5 (the changing bytes 18-19), enc 7 = none
  word7 msdu_start 0x00080083: msdu length 131, ip offset 32; word9 0x100: decap 1 = native wifi
131 = 24 (802.11, no QoS) + 8 (LLC/SNAP) + 99 (EAPOL-Key without key data); 4 frames 1 s apart.
W24H/I/K (202928, 204304, 210106) print nothing: at buf+360 the LLC/SNAP 88 8e is found, then
eapol_note() returns silently on "f[off] != 2" (EAPOL version 1 is legal) - the only silent path left.

Changes (one file, bsd/dev/vayu_wifi_scan.c; diagnostics only, nothing is transmitted):
 - htt_rx_msdu(): check attention MSDU_DONE, length from the in-order descriptor (flame htt_rx),
   decap from msdu_start, 802.11 header length from FC, LLC/SNAP exactly at the header end;
   rx_in_ord_ind offload bit handled (7-byte header, no descriptor).
 - eapol_key(): version 1/2/3 accepted, big-endian key_info/key_len/replay/key data length,
   message number from Pairwise/Ack/MIC/Secure; log `w24: eapol 1/4 ...`.  Nonce never printed.
 - rx_dump(): first msdu and first EAPOL msdu, 96 bytes hex; MAC bytes 0-3 and the nonce masked.
 - one parser per message: vayu_scan_htt_rx parses before the repost; vayu_scan_note_htt only
   when vayu_scan_htt_rx did not (W24K parsed every buffer twice, the second time after the repost).

